    "title": "Crime Stoppers: 2 requests to identify, 3 wanted - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Shajaka Shelton ,\n45 minutes ago\nLANSING, Mich. (WLNS) — This week on Crime Stoppers, police need your help identifying a witness and someone who tried to steal a car, as well as tracking down three people wanted on warrants.\nIf you have information regarding the cases below, call Crime Stoppers of Mid-Michigan at (517) 483-STOP. You can remain anonymous.\nThose who contact Crime Stoppers with information can receive up to a $1,000 award.\nWitness Identification The Lansing Police Department is asking for help identifying someoen who witnessed a felonius vehicular assault that happened on East Edgewood Boulevard on Aug. 3.\nAttempted Car Theft (Crime Stoppers of Mid-Michigan) LPD is also asking for help identifying someone who tried to steal a car from the 900 block of Townsend Street on July 17.\nCori Lee Grout Cori Lee Grout. (Crime Stoppers of Mid-Michigan) Cori Lee Grout, 43, is wanted on a warrant for probation violation and fleeing and eluding a police officer out of Clinton County. She is 5’9″ and 170 lbs, with brown hair and blue eyes.",
    "summary": "LANSING, Mich. (WLNS) — This week on Crime Stoppers, police need your help identifying a witness and someone who tried to steal a car, as well as tracking down three people wanted on warrants. If you have information regarding the cases below, call Crime Stoppers of Mid-Michigan at (517) 483-STOP. Those who contact Crime Stoppers with information can receive up to a $1,000 award. Witness Identification The Lansing Police Department is asking for help identifying someoen who witnessed a felonius vehicular assault that happened on East Edgewood Boulevard on Aug. 3.",
